{
 "regions": [
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "it by रचना. The former i. e. breaking I prefer and take to be the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "meaning in the Prasannarâghava. On the case of दिनानि see",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "Siddh. Kaum. I., 268. बोधका has no particular propriety, probably",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "it means instructors of people.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXIV.—वक्त्रमीक्षसे—comp. St. 95. or 69 प्रत्याशया धावसि = run",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "about through hopes or expectation [of getting some favour]. कुत्र",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "&c. = where and what penance have you practised ? The Stanza",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "occurs also at p. 303 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXV.—See Nîtis'ataka Miscellaneous St. 15.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXVI.—See do. St. 2.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXVII.—See do. Miscellaneous St. 16.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXVIII.—The construction of तदेव in the text is some-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "what difficult. The reading of N. is therefore preferable, only all",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the other five copies are at one. As it stands it must be taken",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "thus शिरोरुहाणां शिरसि सितं वर्णं तदेव पुंसां जरापरिभवस्य स्थानं वीक्ष्य &c. The",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "reading शकल is better as referring to the bit of bone suspended",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "over a चाण्डालकूप.—Vasantatilakâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r9",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XXXIX—समारम्भ = attempts, deeds comp. Gîtâ IV., 19.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "गृहव्यापाराः गृहस्थाश्रमा इत्यर्थः says Râmarshi. अशनि &c. = made of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "adamantine stone. Râmarshi takes it as अशनिर्वज्रं ग्रावाणश्च.—S'i-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "khariṇî.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r10",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XL.—Vasantatilakâ",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r11",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XLI.—खर = sharp. Mallinâtha on Raghu VIII., 9 renders it",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "by तीक्ष्ण.—Vasantatilakâ.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r12",
   "type": "stanza_note",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "St. XLII.—हन्त हर्षे. (Medinî) हरिण see St. 41. वृत्तिः see St. 59.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "For the case of भक्ति see Siddh. Kaum. I., 278. न्त्यै should be न्त्ये—",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "“those whose minds are [fixed] exclusively on internal tranquillity",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "(i. e. self-restraint).” The last line is not very closely connected",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "with the previous three.—S'ikhariṇî.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
